SPP.py file can be found in path /prog1/CSC-4101-Prog1 due to cloning empty repository from Github for remote pair programming

As prompted, we created a scanner, recursive descent parser,
parse tree classes, and printing classes. This scanner reads
tokens from input, parser builds trees using the nodes, and 
the tree then tells which formatting to use for each print.

AI Usage
During the initial programming, we used AI to guide us through concepts connecting the printer, scanner, and parser for better understanding of how the program should tie together.

During our testings, we found that there were 4 failures:

Test0.-d
test3.-d
test9.-d 
test20.scm

For test 20.scm it failed because of formatting issues from code.
We used AI to guide us through to pinpoint the source of the error
and proceeded to change as needed for the tests. 

For Test0.-d, test3.-d, and test9.-d the issue went beyond what was
within the # TODO segments. Inside of the SPP.py file, the error
occurred from the line 
    sys.stdout.write(str(tt))
causing the output to print TokenType.LPAREN when the reference prints LPAREN
we changed it to
    sys.stdout.write(tt.name)
and the failed test was resolved.

